prompt_template:
Create a finished promotional editorial poster in the literal Split Scorched Editorial Poster visual system.

Subject: {SUBJECT}
Action: {SUBJECT_ACTION}
Prop/product: {PRODUCT_OR_PROP}
Location: {LOCATION}
Background: {BACKGROUND_ELEMENTS}
Main text: {MAIN_TEXT}
Secondary text: {SECONDARY_TEXT}
Accent symbol: {ACCENT_SYMBOL}
Wardrobe/styling: {WARDROBE_STYLE}

Preserve these observable style anchors: {STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Do not recreate these source-specific elements: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

Build three interacting planes around a near-even vertical split. Deep plane: the dark left field is an atmospheric charcoal-to-ember environment with smoky red haze, faint horizontal streaks, and a soft echo halo behind the hero head. Middle plane: place the oversized upper-body hero in the upper-left-to-center area, crop the body aggressively at the left and lower frame, and let the shoulders recede into shadow. Foreground plane: place one oversized non-sports prop in front of the lower torso and hands; it must be materially sharper, warmer, and brighter than the hero, begin at lower center, and cross the central seam into the lower cream paper field. Keep the upper and middle-right paper area quiet for the compact headline stack, so type frames the foreground overlap instead of becoming a separate column. Use tall condensed uppercase display type partially obscured by the hero or frame edge, plus a thin rotated metadata line tracking the seam. Restrict color to charcoal, near-black, scarlet, burnt orange, cream paper, and dark espresso. Apply controlled halftone grain, rubbed screenprint ink, soot flecks, red fog, and paper abrasion while preserving crisp material edges on hands, prop, and typography.

Avoid football imagery, helmets, team or league branding, real athlete likenesses, real event copy, watermarks, platform marks, blue or green palette intrusion, glossy commercial polish, muddy texture, extra faces, crowded backgrounds, distorted anatomy, and unreadable typography.
